1
00:04:12,631 --> 00:04:18,631
Meet Fievel. In his search to find his family, he discovered America.

2
00:08:25,263 --> 00:08:31,263
An American Tail is a animation, comedy, adventure film directed by Don Bluth.

3
00:12:37,894 --> 00:12:43,894
A young mouse named Fievel and his family decide to migrate to America,
a "land without cats," at the turn of the 20th century.

4
00:16:50,526 --> 00:16:56,526
But somehow, Fievel ends up in the New World alone and must fend off not only the felines he never
thought he'd have to deal with again but also the loneliness of being away from home.

5
00:21:03,157 --> 00:21:09,157
Fievel Mousekewitz (voice), played by Phillip Glasser.

6
00:25:15,789 --> 00:25:21,789
Mama Mousekewitz (voice), played by Erica Yohn.

7
00:29:28,421 --> 00:29:34,421
Papa Mousekewitz (voice), played by Nehemiah Persoff.

8
00:33:41,052 --> 00:33:47,052
Tanya Mousekewitz (voice), played by Amy Green.

9
00:37:53,684 --> 00:37:59,684
Henri (voice), played by Christopher Plummer.

10
00:42:06,315 --> 00:42:12,315
Warren T. Rat (voice), played by John Finnegan.

11
00:46:18,947 --> 00:46:24,947
An American Tail is a 1986 American animated musical comedy-drama film
directed by Don Bluth and written by Judy Freudberg and Tony Geiss.

12
00:50:31,578 --> 00:50:37,578
The film stars the voices of Phillip Glasser, John Finnegan, Amy Green, Nehemiah
Persoff, Dom DeLuise, Madeline Kahn, and Christopher Plummer.

13
00:54:44,210 --> 00:54:50,210
It is the story of Fievel Mousekewitz and his family as they emigrate from the Russian Empire to the
United States for freedom, but Fievel gets lost and must find a way to reunite with them.

14
00:58:56,842 --> 00:59:02,842
The film was released in the United States on
November 21, 1986, by Universal Pictures.

15
01:03:09,473 --> 01:03:15,473
It received mixed reviews from critics, and grossed $84
million against a budget of $9 million.

16
01:07:22,105 --> 01:07:28,105
The film spawned a franchise, including a sequel, An American Tail: Fievel Goes West (1991), a television series, Fievel's American Tails (1992) and two
direct-to-video sequels, An American Tail: The Treasure of Manhattan Island (1998) and An American Tail: The Mystery of the Night Monster (1999).

17
01:11:34,736 --> 01:11:40,736
The film explores themes of new york city, cat,
immigration, mouse, american dream.

18
01:15:47,368 --> 01:15:53,368
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
